  reason: "WHY RUST: `gunbc run --arg` is the seed CLI kernel. argv is always text (`CliTextValue`); inhabiting a parameter's resolved type is a later, located decision that today lives only in `v1_compiler.cli_run`. Silent String binding was fail-open: `--arg supersedes=2` inhabited Str(\"2\") against an Int parameter. The peel reuses infer's decidable where predicates so `std.types` NonEmptyStr is not a second CLI table. WHY ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing): by PURPOSE — silent wrong binding on every `gunbc run` of a v2 entry, including belt_scm_corrective_integrate_cli and fabric/fci1 NonEmptyStr recipes. It adds no language behaviour. The native CLI door (`v2.cli.compile_cli`) has no `run` verb, so this is not v1 growth for its own sake; it is the only fail-closed inhabitance of the existing seed run verb.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these declarations when a `.dag` driver can receive argv as values AND bind `--arg` text against the entry's resolved parameter types — kernel String/Int/Bool plus declared where-refinements — so the seed peel is not a second authority. That capability is a modeled `gunbc run` on the native CLI, not a wrapper around this Rust. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE IT: copying the peel into another host file; a leaf-name table of aliases; refusing NonEmptyStr instead of walking its declared where-chain.",
  current_boundary: "v1_compiler.cli_run bind_run_args_for_entry (called from v1_compiler.main run_one_function); admissions from cli_arg_admission_from_type_expr over declared_parameter_type_exprs; one bind loop in bind_run_arg_specs_against_admissions; dag/gunbc/run_arg_typed_bind_seed_growth.dag"
}
